The COPY and ADD commands in a Dockerfile are both used to copy files/directories into the image, but there are some key differences between them.

#COPY
Syntax: COPY <src> <dest>
Purpose: Copies files and directories.
Ex:
COPY app/ /demo

Key Points:
1.Only supports copying local files and directories.
2.No automatic unpacking of archives.


#ADD 
Syntax: ADD <src> <dest>
Purpose: Like COPY, but with extra features.
Ex:
ADD demo.tar.gz /demo

Key points:
1. automatically unpack local .tar, .tar.gz, .tar.bz2, .tar.xz archives.
2.Can fetch files from remote URLs.

ADD https://lnkd.in/gTxs3dQG /demo
